  grapes="Chardonnay, Shiraz, Semillon, Cabernet Sauvignon, Durif, Pinot Grigio",
  summary="The Murrumbidgee Irrigation Area around Griffith and Leeton, opened in 1912 and settled largely by Italian families, crushes about 235,000 to 300,000 tonnes a year. Casella's [yellow tail], launched in 2001, became the best-selling imported wine brand in the United States within a few years. The region's one great wine is a sweet one: De Bortoli's Noble One botrytis Semillon, first made in 1982, showed that the morning humidity around Griffith could produce noble rot in autumn.",
