  summary="A plateau of granite boulders around Stanthorpe and Ballandean on the New South Wales border, at 600 to 1,300 m, registered in 2002. The altitude makes it cool despite a latitude of 28 to 29 degrees south. Italian migrants grew grapes here from the 1920s; today about 300 ha support boutique wineries, and the 'Strange Birds' trail promotes unusual varieties.",
